.Dd October 24, 2026
.Dt XCODE-SELECT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xcode-select
.Nd query and select a developer directory
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl p | -print-path
.Nm
.Fl s | -switch
.Ar directory
.Nm
.Fl r | -reset
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fl p
prints the effective absolute developer directory using the same precedence
and validation as
.Xr xcrun 1 .
Queries never modify the selection.
.Pp
.Fl s
requires an absolute existing directory and atomically replaces
.Pa /var/db/xcode_select_link
with a symlink to it.
It ignores
.Ev DEVELOPER_DIR
when storing the selection.
The parent directory must exist and permit writes.
A dangling selection symlink may be replaced;
a regular file or directory is rejected and preserved.
.Pp
.Fl r
removes only the selection symlink.
An absent selector succeeds; a regular file or directory fails unchanged.
Without
.Ev DEVELOPER_DIR ,
the next query validates the default
.Pa /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools .
.Pp
.Fl h
prints usage.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Success returns 0, operational errors return 1 and syntax errors return 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xcrun 1
.Sh NOTES
The source directory's README.md specifies the supported contract.
Installation, downloading and other Apple options are not implemented.
